# SABOTAGE: issue #11 / D-17 — the failed attempt is billed onto the in-memory `%Run{}`
# struct only, never written. The D-13 budget re-check at the retry boundary reads the run
# ROW through `reload!/1`, so it cannot see the bill: a failed attempt that by itself
# exhausted the budget folds and retries anyway — the knowing overrun D-17 rules out.
#
# Flips the D-17 test. The plain billing test can stay GREEN under this sabotage (the
# struct carries the bill on to a later committing site that writes it), which is exactly
# why a struct-only bill looks correct until the budget boundary is what reads it.
# Re-anchored for the #11 follow-up: `bill_failed_attempt` now also stamps the turn row
# (it takes and returns `turn_row`), so the surrounding context moved. Same edit.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/ai/agent_durability_test.exs
